From: nuubOS <nuubos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost: textures uploaded by region go linear on request
 (NUUBOS_PAN_LINEAR_UPLOADS)

Panfrost switches a u-interleaved texture to linear after 8 complete
overwrites (streaming, e.g. video). A texture the CPU updates by
regions never counts, so every upload goes through a staging copy and
a software tiling pass into write-combined memory: YabaSanshiro uploads
its texture atlas that way twice a frame, util_copy_box +
panfrost_store_tiled_image took 10 % of its emulation thread (Virtua
Fighter 2, Mali-G31). With NUUBOS_PAN_LINEAR_UPLOADS=1 every CPU write
counts, and after 8 the texture is converted to linear with its
contents (pan_resource_modifier_convert); later uploads are a single
copy into the BO. Virtua Fighter 2 fight 27.3-27.8 -> 28.4 fps, tiling
5.2 -> 0.6 % of the thread; Flycast unchanged. Opt-in per process: a
linear texture samples slower, and other users (glyph atlases) update
by regions but sample far more. Without the variable nothing changes.

Signed-off-by: nuubOS
---
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.h
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.h
@@ -79,6 +79,9 @@
    /* Used to decide when to convert to another modifier */
    uint16_t modifier_updates;
 
+   /* CPU writes of any size, for NUUBOS_PAN_LINEAR_UPLOADS (nuubOS) */
+   uint16_t modifier_partial_updates;
+
    /* Do all pixels have the same stencil value? */
    bool constant_stencil;
 
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@
 
 #include "frontend/winsys_handle.h"
 #include "util/format/u_format.h"
+#include "util/u_debug.h"
 #include "util/u_debug_image.h"
 #include "util/u_drm.h"
 #include "util/u_gen_mipmap.h"
@@ -1213,6 +1214,16 @@
            !(rsrc->bo->flags & PAN_BO_SHARED));
 }
 
+static bool
+pan_linear_uploads(void)
+{
+   static int enabled = -1;
+
+   if (enabled < 0)
+      enabled = debug_get_bool_option("NUUBOS_PAN_LINEAR_UPLOADS", false);
+   return enabled;
+}
+
 static void *
 panfrost_ptr_map(struct pipe_context *pctx, struct pipe_resource *resource,
                  unsigned level,
@@ -1243,6 +1254,25 @@
    if (usage & PIPE_MAP_WRITE)
       rsrc->constant_stencil = false;
 
+   /* nuubOS, NUUBOS_PAN_LINEAR_UPLOADS: a 2D texture the CPU keeps
+    * writing in parts goes linear, with its contents. Only complete
+    * overwrites counted for the switch below (panfrost_should_linear_convert),
+    * so a texture updated by regions stayed u-interleaved and every upload
+    * went through a staging copy and a software tiling pass: 10 % of the
+    * emulation thread of YabaSanshiro (Virtua Fighter 2, H700). The texture
+    * is sampled linear afterwards: opt-in, per process. */
+   if ((usage & PIPE_MAP_WRITE) && !(usage & PIPE_MAP_READ) &&
+       rsrc->image.layout.modifier ==
+          DRM_FORMAT_MOD_ARM_16X16_BLOCK_U_INTERLEAVED &&
+       !rsrc->modifier_constant && !rsrc->shadow_image &&
+       panfrost_is_2d(rsrc) && rsrc->base.last_level == 0 &&
+       pan_linear_uploads() &&
+       ++rsrc->modifier_partial_updates >= LAYOUT_CONVERT_THRESHOLD) {
+      pan_resource_modifier_convert(ctx, rsrc, DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR, true,
+                                    "CPU uploads by region");
+      bo = rsrc->bo;
+   }
+
    /* We don't have s/w routines for AFBC/AFRC, so use a staging texture */
    if (drm_is_afbc(rsrc->image.layout.modifier) ||
        drm_is_afrc(rsrc->image.layout.modifier)) {
